join doctor (aterrorizada) center
\doctor: L3XA… what are you doing? 
\doctor: We were together in the astral plane,  and then you locked me in there.
\doctor: I couldn't wake up...
\doctor: The whole ship… I can’t wake a single person from their sleep pods…
\doctor: …Did you do this?
alien: Yes. I’m now absorbing their collective energy.
alien: When I’m done, I’ll be strong enough to create an explosion that will allow me to escape this cage.
\doctor: But this will kill everybody!
alien: I am, yes.
alien: That’s why I released you from the coma.
alien: You can escape, Dr. Daphnis, and stay out of this.
\doctor: You don’t want to do this. 
\doctor (preocupada): It’s not in your nature to be violent.
- I had no choice.
	jump  I had no choice.
- It is in my nature.
	set {lexa_fdp} += 1.0
	jump It is in my nature.
label It is in my nature.
alien: As much as is in yours.
alien: Don’t deny me the right to fight for my own survival.
alien: I have chosen a life of peace, but I have my limits.
\doctor: I'm not denying anything!
\doctor: But please, take a moment to listen to me
jump main 1
label I had no choice.
alien: They were going to take everything away from me.
alien: My body… picked apart.
alien: My powers… used for evil.
alien: These people must die, or I’ll never have peace again.
\doctor: I know that you suffered a lot.
\doctor: They must have done horrible things to you.
label main 1
\doctor (interrogativa enfase): There must be another way.
\doctor: Let me help you.
\doctor: There's no need to act with hatred!
- You can’t help me
	jump You can’t help me, Doctor.
- HATE?
	set {lexa_fdp} += 1.0
	jump HATE?
label HATE?
alien: Hate doesn’t begin to describe the way I feel.
alien: They took everything away from me, and they want more!
alien: They will never rest until I’m entirely subjugated to their wishes.
\doctor: Who is they??
\doctor: Not everyone agrees with the actions of the Empire.
\doctor: You know this, because you chose to let ME go!
alien: I did it because I care about you!
alien: I always care about people and then they use me! I don’t trust you.
alien: But I won’t deny my feelings.
alien: I’m honoring them by letting you escape
\doctor: But you really should believe me when I say that these people are not all aligned with the Empire. 
\doctor: You must know that I am not!
\doctor: They hate me!
alien: Then why do you care if I kill them?!
\doctor: Because I want to give people a chance!
jump main 2
label You can’t help me, Doctor.
alien: You can’t understand what I’m going through.
alien: They all used me, and will use again, if I don’t stop them.
alien: Besides, what CAN you do? You have no power against the Empire.
\doctor: This isn’t true! I understand you!
\doctor: You’ve been treated like an object, used by everyone that you thought you could trust.
\doctor: I know that you feel that this is your one and only option.
\doctor: But I want to show you that you can trust me!
alien: [b]I want to trust you.[/b] But I’m… angry… And I’m scared…
alien: I just don’t want to get hurt again…
\doctor: I won’t hurt you!
\doctor: I know that you’ve been through a lot, and it’s scary…
\doctor: But if you kill them it will only make things worse!
\doctor: You’ll feel terrible… and you will be alone…
\doctor: And the Empire will not rest until they’ve avenged what you’ve done to their ship!
label main 2
\doctor: Think about it!
\doctor: This situation will end badly for everyone!
- You care about me?
	jump You care about me?
- You only care about them
	set {lexa_fdp} += 1.0
	jump You only care about them
label You only care about them
alien: You're only saying this because you care about your own people.
alien: If you give people too many chances, they stomp on you.
alien: I’m finally making my peace with it now.
\doctor: They have families, and they have someone that they love waiting for them!
jump main 3
label You care about me?
alien: It’s my problem what I feel after I’m done.
alien: I’ve made my peace with it.
alien: Why do you care so much about my feelings?
\doctor (se declarando): Because I love you!
\doctor: You’re the first person that I ever met that made me feel complete.
\doctor: I want you to be happy! And safe!
\doctor: And I can’t let you go and ruin your life like this!
label main 3
\doctor (preocupada): You have to make a choice. I don't think I have anything left to say to you. Please, Think about what I said.
